NAME
     dd - copy blocks

SYNOPSIS
     dd [if=FILE] [of=FILE] [bs=N] [count=N] [skip=N] [seek=N] [conv=...]

DESCRIPTION
     dd copies blocks from one file to another, and says how many it
     moved. It is how to write an image to a device, make a file of
     zeroes, or read a few blocks from the middle of something.

OPTIONS
     if=FILE    read from FILE (standard input by default)
     of=FILE    write to FILE (standard output by default)
     bs=N       the block size; N may end in k, M or G
     count=N    copy N blocks
     skip=N     skip N blocks of the input
     seek=N     skip N blocks of the output
     conv=...   notrunc, sync, fsync

EXAMPLES
     dd if=/dev/zero of=/tmp/z bs=4096 count=256
     dd if=/dev/vda of=/tmp/first.img bs=512 count=2048

SEE ALSO
     cp(1), truncate(1), mkimage(1)
